WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.072
Before creating a view, make four decisions.

00:00:03.072 --> 00:00:06.502
Choose a meaningful name. Define the row grain.

00:00:06.502 --> 00:00:12.152
Choose the columns intentionally. Then write the SELECT that implements that interface.

00:00:12.152 --> 00:00:16.507
Starting with the contract makes the SQL easier to evaluate.

00:00:16.507 --> 00:00:21.627
When reading the example, do not read punctuation one character at a time.

00:00:21.627 --> 00:00:26.117
Start with the purpose of the query, then identify the input rows, the operation being applied,

00:00:26.117 --> 00:00:30.592
and the shape of the expected output.

00:00:30.592 --> 00:00:36.607
In a real setting such as a governance project limiting which columns different users can access,

00:00:36.607 --> 00:00:42.662
this habit makes code reviews much easier because you can explain what the query is supposed to guarantee

00:00:42.662 --> 00:00:44.912
before discussing syntax.

00:00:44.912 --> 00:00:50.943
After running it, inspect a few records manually and check that the result matches that explanation.
